# 11. Funding Architecture

American conservation is financed through multiple channels.

A simplified structure is:

```text
Federal Appropriations
        │
        ├── Federal Agencies
        │
        ├── State Grants
        │
        └── Tribal Programs

Dedicated Federal Revenues
        │
        ├── Wildlife Restoration
        ├── Sport Fish Restoration
        └── Other Dedicated Programs

State Revenues
        │
        ├── General Funds
        ├── Licenses & Fees
        └── State Bonds / Dedicated Revenues

Private & Nongovernmental
        │
        ├── Foundations
        ├── Donations
        ├── Land Trusts
        └── Partnerships
```

This diversified structure creates resilience.

It also makes it difficult to determine:

> **How much does America spend on conservation as a whole?**

A later project deliverable should therefore attempt to construct a **National Conservation Funding Inventory**.

