# 12. Ecological Systems Versus Political Jurisdictions

One of the fundamental structural characteristics of conservation governance is the mismatch between ecological and political boundaries.

Consider a migratory species:

```text
Breeding habitat
      ↓
State land
      ↓
Federal land
      ↓
Private land
      ↓
Another state
      ↓
International boundary
      ↓
Wintering habitat
```

Or a watershed:

```text
Headwaters
    ↓
County
    ↓
State
    ↓
Second State
    ↓
Estuary
    ↓
Federal waters
```

The ecological system is continuous.

Governance is not.

This creates a recurring requirement for coordination.

